title: Milestone_1
---
Your phone rings the second the girls clock out. She's been waiting.
Jennifer: Day five. Let's see what you've got.
Jennifer: {$profit}. Huh. I had money on you crying in a sand dune by now.
Jennifer: Next milestone is {$goal} by day ten. Don't get comfortable, comfortable people get *replaced*.
-> I'll double it. For you.
    <<set $corporate += 1>>
    Jennifer: Save the charm for the board. They're the ones who sign your checks.
-> The girls did all the work.
    <<set $workers += 1>>
    Jennifer: The girls are a line item. *You're* the one I'm calling. #scolding
===
title: Milestone_2
---
Jennifer: Day ten. {$profit}. I've seen worse. I've *fired* worse. #scolding
Jennifer: Last one. {$goal} by day fifteen. Hit it and we'll talk about your future. Miss it and we'll talk about your severance.
<<if $overtime_week>>
Jennifer: And you can send the drones home at five again. Don't make me regret it.
<<overtime_every_day false>>
<<set $overtime_week to false>>
<<endif>>
===
title: Milestone_3
---
Day fifteen. The phone rings once, and you pick up.
Jennifer: Moment of truth. {$profit}.
Jennifer: ...Well. I'll be.
===
title: Ending_Fired
---
Your phone rings. You let it ring twice, which doesn't help.
Jennifer: I'm looking at the numbers and the numbers are looking at me. {$profit}. #scolding
Jennifer: That's not a profit, that's a cry for help. #scolding
Jennifer: You're fired. Leave the drones, they're Licorich property. #scolding
-> Can I at least keep a croissant?
    Jennifer: Put it back. #scolding
-> They're not drones. They have names.
    Jennifer: And now they'll have a new manager. Goodbye.
The jet comes back the next morning. This time the pilot turns the engines off, just to watch you walk.
===
title: Ending_Promoted
---
Jennifer: You actually did it. Three for three.
Jennifer: Pack your bags. You're coming to Licorich headquarters. Corner office, no windows, the works.
<<if not $knows_jennifer>>
Jennifer: Oh, and it's Jennifer. Not Corpo-sama. You've earned that much.
<<set $knows_jennifer to true>>
<<endif>>
Red Velvet: Congratulations, boss! We'll...erm...keep the ovens warm for the next one.
The girls are already sweeping sand off the stall when the jet lands. Nobody waves.
===
title: Ending_Jennifer
---
Jennifer: You actually did it. Three for three.
Jennifer: The board wants you at headquarters. Top floor. The office next to mine.
<<if not $knows_jennifer>>
Jennifer: And it's Jennifer. Not Corpo-sama. You've earned that much.
<<set $knows_jennifer to true>>
<<endif>>
Jennifer: I'm also told I'm allowed one personal hire this year.
Jennifer: That was a joke. Mostly. I've been told I'm bad at those. By the board.
-> Is this you asking me to dinner?
    Jennifer: It's me telling you there's a table for two at eight. Don't be late, I bill by the hour.
-> I'd follow you anywhere, Jennifer.
    Jennifer: ...Don't make it weird. #scolding
    Jennifer: Eight o'clock. Wear something without sand on it.
Red Velvet: Congratulations, boss. We'll...erm...keep the ovens warm for the next one. #cringe
The jet lands at sunset. She's on it. She says she was in the area. Licorich doesn't have an area out here.
===
title: Ending_Red_Velvet
---
Red Velvet: Erm...boss? Before corporate calls back. We need to talk.
Red Velvet: The girls and I took a vote. We're a union now. Fair wages, shade, and five o'clock means five o'clock.
Red Velvet: They voted on something else too. I...erm...wasn't allowed to vote on that one. #cringe
Red Velvet: They want you to stay. And I want...I also want you to stay. Not as our boss. Well, as our boss. But also not.
Your phone rings again.
Jennifer: What is this I'm hearing about a *union*?! #scolding
-> I'm staying. With them.
    Jennifer: Then enjoy the sand. That's all you'll be getting from Licorich. #scolding
-> Can I call you back? I'm busy.
    Jennifer: Don't you dare hang up on m- #scolding
You hang up. Red Velvet is holding out half a burnt croissant.
Red Velvet: It's the best one. I burnt it myself.
-> Share it with her.
    You split it. It's terrible. You both eat the whole thing anyway.
-> Ask her to dinner.
    Red Velvet: Dinner? Out here? There's only the stall. ...The stall's perfect.
The jet never comes. You stop listening for it.
===
title: Ending_Unionized
---
Red Velvet: Erm...boss? Before corporate calls back. We need to talk. #cringe
Red Velvet: The girls and I took a vote. We're a union now. Fair wages, shade, and five o'clock means five o'clock.
Red Velvet: Also Honey says we keep the burnt ones. And Mocha says *all* the burnt ones.
Red Velvet: And...we'd like you to stay. As our boss. If you want.
Your phone rings again.
Jennifer: What is this I'm hearing about a *union*?! #scolding
-> I'm with them.
    Jennifer: Then you can stay out there with them. Enjoy the sand. #scolding
-> It was like this when I got here.
    Jennifer: Of course it was. Don't bother coming back. #scolding
The jet never comes. The croissants are better than ever.
===
